														<r3d:remarks>National funding agencies in all participating countries are required to contribute to the central coordination costs, led by the ESS Core Scientific Team (CST). These are composed of a basic membership fee and an additional amount, calculated according to the GDP of each country. In addition, each country covers the cost of fieldwork and national coordination.
Prior to the award of ERIC status, the ESS was funded on a round-by-round basis. The central coordination and design was funded through the European Commission, the European Science Foundation (ESF) and national funding councils.
The ESS has also been a beneficiary of several projects funded by the European Commission.</r3d:remarks>
